  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1121 AM MDT Wed Oct 28 2026\n\nMostly calm and quiet weather in store today. Isolated thunderstorms \npossible this afternoon and early evening in Hudspeth and southern \nOtero counties. A slug of moisture will continue pushing north into \nour area on Thursday allowing PW values to reach a near record \nbreaking value of around 1\". A shortwave will act as the lifting \nmechanism for storms starting Thursday morning and persisting all \nday. Expecting showery activity with some embedded thunderstorms. \nThe strongest storms will be capable of producing flash flooding. \nStorm chances persists into Friday. \n\nA brief break on Saturday but a much deeper trough will be the \nlifting mechanism for storms Sunday and into portions of Monday. \nExpect areawide rain chances Sunday. PWs will be well above normal \nagain for this time of year on Sunday nearing around 0.9\" to 1.0\". \nBetter forcing will increase the flooding threat. Winds will be \nslightly breezy Sunday becoming even breezier Monday. Moisture looks \nto quickly get shoved out behind this large upper trough Monday. \nTemperatures also look to take a dip too on Tuesday behind the low \nwith lowland highs in the upper 60s and low 70s.",
